LM-2 and CR-78 kit definitions are 808-sample aliases, not real recordings.

Surfaced by the TASK-224 research report. Looking at
src/engine/kits.c:

  - "CR-78" (rows 105-117): all 8 slot paths point at
    samples/808/03.* and samples/808/01.CB/RS/MT.*  — these
    are 808 samples, not Roland CR-78 recordings.

  - "LM-2"  (rows 119-131): all 8 slot paths point at
    samples/808/05.* and samples/808/01.LC/MC/LT.*  — 808 again,
    not LinnDrum LM-2.

The kit *names* in the dropdown are misleading — users picking
"LinnDrum" expect that distinctive 80s pop sound, not a tweaked
808.

## Two paths to resolve

### Quick: rename the aliases honestly
Rename the entries to "808 alt 03" and "808 alt 05" (or similar)
so the names match what's playing. No new samples needed; binary
size unchanged.

### Better: ship real samples
Replace with actual public-domain LinnDrum LM-2 and CR-78 recordings
from the Oramics `sampled` repo (verified MIT-licensed code, PD
audio per the report). Adds ~1.5 MB to the install. See
docs/research/kit-expansion.md sections "1. LinnDrum LM-2 (proper)"
and "4. Roland CR-78 (real samples)" for source URLs.

The "Better" path is the recommended one — it's the actual fix.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] LM-2 kit slots load real LinnDrum samples (or rename to match
      what's playing)
- [ ] CR-78 kit slots load real CR-78 samples (or rename)
- [ ] samples/LICENSE.md updated to credit added sources
- [ ] Existing project files don't break (kit_load uses base_dir +
      relative paths, so renaming files is safe; renaming the kit
      *name* string only affects the dropdown label)

## Test Plan
- [ ] Switch to LM-2 in the kit dropdown, hit play — should sound
      like the LinnDrum, not the 808
- [ ] Switch to CR-78 — should sound like the CR-78
- [ ] Reset to Defaults still works (kit 0 = 808 unchanged)
